{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Seven cows.</b> An allusion to famine and to satiety, because they plow the field of grain." "<b>And they stood by the cows.</b> They lingered by them — they did not devour them immediately. The interpretation: the famine would not consume the earth's grain immediately, as it is written: ״ובכל ארץ מצרים היה לחם״."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 41, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:08:10.406340099Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}